      "template": "<div lang=\"en\" style=\"width:100%; min-height:100vh; background:#0a0a09; font-family:'Cormorant Garamond', serif; box-sizing:border-box;\">\n\n  \n\n  \n\n  <header>\n    <nav aria-label=\"Breadcrumb\" style=\"max-width:1180px; margin:0 auto; padding:56px 24px 0;\">\n      <a href=\"/en/collection/colonial-paper-money/\" style=\"display:inline-block; color:#e7ddc4; text-decoration:none; font-size:15px; letter-spacing:0.08em;\">&larr; Colonial coin catalog</a>\n    </nav>\n  </header>\n\n  <main data-pagefind-meta=\"url:/en/collection/colonial-paper-money/profile-benjamin-franklin/\" id=\"main-content\" tabindex=\"-1\" style=\"max-width:1180px; margin:0 auto; padding:24px 24px 80px; outline:none;\">\n\n    <div style=\"background:#d8d2cd; border:1px solid rgba(10,10,9,0.08); border-radius:3px; padding:clamp(28px,4vw,64px); box-shadow:0 30px 70px rgba(0,0,0,0.45);\">\n\n      <div style=\"display:flex; flex-direction:column; align-items:center;\">\n\n        <div style=\"text-align:center; max-width:720px; margin:0 auto 40px;\">\n          <span style=\"display:block; font-size:14px; letter-spacing:0.22em; text-transform:uppercase; color:#5c4e33; margin-bottom:14px;\">Historical Profile &middot; American Colonial Currency</span>\n          <h1 style=\"font-family:'Montenegrin Gothic One', serif; font-weight:400; font-size:clamp(28px,4vw,44px); line-height:1.1; letter-spacing:0.01em; color:#1c1a15; margin:0 0 12px;\">Benjamin Franklin</h1>\n          <p style=\"font-size:clamp(19px,2vw,23px); font-style:italic; color:#4a4331; margin:0;\">Boston, 1706 &mdash; Philadelphia, 1790</p>\n        </div>\n\n        <div style=\"width:100%; max-width:400px; display:flex; flex-direction:column; gap:14px; margin:0 auto 56px;\">\n          <div style=\"width:100%; aspect-ratio:960/1171; border:1px solid rgba(10,10,9,0.12); overflow:hidden;\">\n            <picture style=\"display:block; width:100%; height:100%;\">\n              <source srcset=\"/uploads/franklin-portrait-duplessis-v2-480.webp 480w, /uploads/franklin-portrait-duplessis-v2.webp 960w\" sizes=\"(max-width: 448px) calc(100vw - 48px), 400px\" type=\"image/webp\" />\n              <img src=\"/uploads/franklin-portrait-duplessis-v2.jpg\" alt=\"Oil portrait of Benjamin Franklin, seated, in a gray waistcoat and white ruffled shirt\" width=\"960\" height=\"1171\" decoding=\"async\" fetchpriority=\"high\" style=\"width:100%; height:100%; object-fit:cover; display:block;\">\n            </picture>\n          </div>\n          <div style=\"text-align:center; font-size:14px; line-height:1.6; color:#5c4e33; font-style:italic;\">\n            <span style=\"display:block;\">Benjamin Franklin</span>\n            <span style=\"display:block;\">By Joseph-Siffred Duplessis &mdash; public domain</span>\n          </div>\n        </div>\n\n        <div style=\"width:100%; max-width:760px;\">\n          <div style=\"display:flex; flex-direction:column;\">\n            <div style=\"display:grid; grid-template-columns:200px 1fr; gap:6px 20px; padding:14px 0; border-top:1px solid rgba(10,10,9,0.12);\">\n              <span style=\"font-size:14px; letter-spacing:0.1em; text-transform:uppercase; color:#5c4e33;\">Birth</span>\n              <span style=\"font-size:19px; color:#221f19;\">January 17, 1706 &mdash; Boston, Massachusetts Bay Province</span>\n            </div>\n            <div style=\"display:grid; grid-template-columns:200px 1fr; gap:6px 20px; padding:14px 0; border-top:1px solid rgba(10,10,9,0.12);\">\n              <span style=\"font-size:14px; letter-spacing:0.1em; text-transform:uppercase; color:#5c4e33;\">Death</span>\n              <span style=\"font-size:19px; color:#221f19;\">April 17, 1790 &mdash; Philadelphia, Pennsylvania</span>\n            </div>\n            <div style=\"display:grid; grid-template-columns:200px 1fr; gap:6px 20px; padding:14px 0; border-top:1px solid rgba(10,10,9,0.12);\">\n              <span style=\"font-size:14px; letter-spacing:0.1em; text-transform:uppercase; color:#5c4e33;\">Profession</span>\n              <span style=\"font-size:19px; color:#221f19;\">Printer, Scientist, Inventor and Statesman</span>\n            </div>\n            <div style=\"display:grid; grid-template-columns:200px 1fr; gap:6px 20px; padding:14px 0; border-top:1px solid rgba(10,10,9,0.12); border-bottom:1px solid rgba(10,10,9,0.12);\">\n              <span style=\"font-size:14px; letter-spacing:0.1em; text-transform:uppercase; color:#5c4e33;\">Key Role</span>\n              <span style=\"font-size:19px; color:#221f19;\">Founding Father of the United States; pioneer printer of anti-counterfeiting techniques on American colonial currency</span>\n            </div>\n          </div>\n\n          <section style=\"margin-top:44px;\">\n            <h2 style=\"font-size:15px; letter-spacing:0.2em; text-transform:uppercase; color:#5c4e33; font-weight:600; margin:0 0 14px; font-style:normal;\">1. The Philadelphia Printer</h2>\n            <p style=\"font-size:19px; line-height:1.65; color:#332e22; margin:0 0 12px;\">Before becoming the scientist and diplomat we know today, Benjamin Franklin was primarily a printer by trade. After an apprenticeship in Boston, he settled in Philadelphia, where his printing press prospered thanks to publications such as the<em>Pennsylvania Gazette</em>and the celebrated<em>Poor Richard&rsquo;s Almanack</em>.</p>\n            <p style=\"font-size:19px; line-height:1.65; color:#332e22; margin:0;\">His workshop also became one of the leading printers of paper money for several American colonies, a lucrative business requiring great technical responsibility in an era of endemic counterfeiting.</p>\n          </section>\n\n          <section style=\"margin-top:36px;\">\n            <h2 style=\"font-size:15px; letter-spacing:0.2em; text-transform:uppercase; color:#5c4e33; font-weight:600; margin:0 0 14px; font-style:normal;\">2. The Innovation of the Natural Leaf</h2>\n            <p style=\"font-size:19px; line-height:1.65; color:#332e22; margin:0 0 12px;\">Franklin and his printing partners developed one of the most ingenious anti-counterfeiting measures for colonial paper money: transfer printing.<strong style=\"color:#1c1a15;\">natural leaves</strong>. The ribbing pattern of each real sheet is microscopically unique and impossible to replicate by hand or by conventional engraving, making each banknote virtually unforgeable with the technology of the time.</p>\n            <p style=\"font-size:19px; line-height:1.65; color:#332e22; margin:0;\">This technique was adopted in the issues of several colonies, including New Jersey, and is today considered an early antecedent of biometric security applied to paper money.</p>\n          </section>\n\n          <section style=\"margin-top:36px;\">\n            <h2 style=\"font-size:15px; letter-spacing:0.2em; text-transform:uppercase; color:#5c4e33; font-weight:600; margin:0 0 14px; font-style:normal;\">3. From Printer to Founding Father</h2>\n            <p style=\"font-size:19px; line-height:1.65; color:#332e22; margin:0 0 12px;\">Franklin combined his publishing career with prolific scientific work &mdash;his experiments with electricity and invention of the lightning rod brought him international fame&mdash; and diplomacy, representing the American colonies in London and later the independent United States at the French court.</p>\n            <p style=\"font-size:19px; line-height:1.65; color:#332e22; margin:0;\">He signed the nation's three most important founding documents: the Declaration of Independence (1776), the Treaty of Alliance with France (1778), and the Constitution of the United States (1787).</p>\n          </section>\n\n          <section style=\"margin-top:36px;\">\n            <h2 style=\"font-size:15px; letter-spacing:0.2em; text-transform:uppercase; color:#5c4e33; font-weight:600; margin:0 0 14px; font-style:normal;\">4. Numismatic Legacy</h2>\n            <p style=\"font-size:19px; line-height:1.65; color:#332e22; margin:0;\">The natural-leaf technique that Franklin helped popularize can be seen on the reverse of the<a href=\"/en/collection/colonial-paper-money/new-jersey-6-shillings-1776/\">New Jersey Six Shillings (1776)</a>of this collection. Franklin also figures, centuries later, as the permanent portrait on the American $100 bill.</p>\n          </section>\n\n          <div style=\"margin-top:44px; padding-top:20px; border-top:1px solid rgba(10,10,9,0.12);\">\n            <h2 style=\"font-size:13px; letter-spacing:0.14em; text-transform:uppercase; color:#5c4e33; font-weight:600; margin:0 0 10px; font-style:normal;\">Notes</h2>\n            <p style=\"font-size:14px; line-height:1.6; color:#5c4e33; margin:0;\">Biography based on standard historical sources on the life of Benjamin Franklin and numismatic references on the natural leaf printing technique on American colonial currency.</p>\n          </div>\n\n        </div>\n      </div>\n    </div>\n  </main>\n\n  \n\n</div>",
